// Azure Speech concurrency utilisation, 15-minute bins (DIAAT-282). Recording:
// workload and capacity.
//
// Measure: running recording batch jobs as a share of the Azure Speech concurrent-jobs
//   limit.
// Formula: 100 * max(value) per bin, across replicas and samples (100 = at the limit).
// Source: gauge transcription.speech.concurrency.utilisation = running jobs /
//   SPEECH_CONCURRENT_JOBS_LIMIT, exported by transcribe-api-worker. Recording-only
//   metric, so no area filter: metric dimensions do not carry hmcts.area (decision 1).
//   Never sampled (OD2).
// Caveats: emitted ONLY when SPEECH_CONCURRENT_JOBS_LIMIT is set on the worker; no data
//   means the limit is not configured. Max across replicas, never sum. Dictation's live
//   Speech sessions are not counted against this limit here.
customMetrics
| where name == "transcription.speech.concurrency.utilisation"
| summarize utilisation_pct = round(100.0 * max(value), 1) by bin(timestamp, 15m)
| order by timestamp asc
